  "worked_solution": "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{5}\\cdot {4}^{4x-1} & \\le {4}^{4x+4} \\\\ {x}^{5}\\cdot {4}^{4x-1}-{4}^{4x+4} & \\le 0 \\\\ {x}^{5}\\cdot {4}^{4x-1}-{4}^{5}\\cdot {4}^{4x-1} & \\le 0 \\\\ ({x}^{5}-{4}^{5})\\cdot {4}^{4x-1} & \\le 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${4}^{4x-1}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{({x}^{5}-{4}^{5})\\cdot {4}^{4x-1}}{{4}^{4x-1}} & \\le \\frac{0}{{4}^{4x-1}} \\\\ ({x}^{5}-{4}^{5}) & \\le 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve this inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{5}-{4}^{5}) & \\le 0 \\\\ {x}^{5} & \\le {4}^{5} \\\\ \\sqrt[5]{{x}^{5}} & \\le \\sqrt[5]{{4}^{5}} \\\\ x & \\le 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality above is $x\\le 4.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
